title: The server finds each skgrepo's own gitrepo inside the outer one, whether its '.git' is a folder or, in a clone, a file.
pid: 2267effa-ba10-4e18-a1e2-f17bf47c561e
body: |2-
  It opens a skgrepo with git2's 'Repository::discover' from the
  skgrepo's folder, which stops at the first '.git'. Seen working, save
  and commit, on a copy of 'data/claude/' as it now is and on a fresh
  clone: each commit landed in the skgrepo, and the outer repo only saw
  its pin move. 'specialist.sh up' tested '-d notes/.git', which a clone
  fails; it now tests '-e'.
  The other side of it: a folder inside 'data/claude/' or 'data/jeff/'
  with no '.git' of its own now belongs to the outer repo, for the
  server's 'discover' and for every 'git -C'. So an owned skgrepo must
  be 'git init'ed before its server starts, as 'specialist.sh up' does,
  and the push script stops on a folder that is not its own gitrepo:
  otherwise 'gh repo create --source' would push claude-config, public.
